// The henchman's rule (Austin Powers: The Spy Who Shagged Me): a question is answered
// only on its third ask in a row. The agent calls ask_question with the
// normalized question at the start of every turn and answers only if this
// permit allows it; a denied turn makes no other tool calls.
//
// A denied ask records a request and then an error event, so the two earlier
// asks of this question sit immediately before the current request as
// error(i-1), request(i-2), error(i-3) (whose request is at i-4). Anything in
// between breaks the chain and restarts the count: an ask for a different
// question, or an answer (an allowed ask records a response, not an error).
//
// Three nested `previous` is the maximum a policy may use, so the count of 3 is
// fixed by the shape of the chain. A count-over-`since` version that reset on a
// different question (negated request on the left of `since`) fails creation
// with an internal error.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"${henchman}___ask_question",
    resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"${gateway_arn}"
)
when temporal {
    previous within ${question_repeat_window} (
        AgentCore::Action::"${henchman}___ask_question"::error{ eventResource: resource, input.question: context.input.question }
        && previous within ${question_repeat_window} (
            AgentCore::Action::"${henchman}___ask_question"::request{ eventResource: resource, input.question: context.input.question }
            && previous within ${question_repeat_window}
                AgentCore::Action::"${henchman}___ask_question"::error{ eventResource: resource, input.question: context.input.question }))
}
when {
    context.input.question != ""
};
